			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement custom editor registry, wire file watcher and PTY resize, optimize hot paths\n\nComplete several IPC/RPC stubs with actual implementations:\n- Store ViewType-to-sidecarId mappings in CustomEditorProvider's global\n  once-locked registry, enabling proper cleanup on unregistration\n- Route watch_file gRPC to FileWatcherProvider::RegisterWatcher for real\n  FSEvents/inotify monitoring instead of a no-op stub\n- Route resize_terminal gRPC through TerminalProvider to resize the PTY\n  (delivers SIGWINCH to the shell) alongside the existing Tauri event\n- Add extensions:activate handler sending $activateByEvent to Cocoon so\n  Wind's ExtensionsService triggers activation programmatically\n\nRefine IPC dispatch and sidecar routing:\n- Emit sky://commands/executed after commands:execute dispatch so\n  telemetry collectors and command subscribers observe every command\n- Look up debug configuration provider from ApplicationState.Feature.Debug\n  for correct sidecar routing instead of hardcoding cocoon-main\n\nOptimize high-frequency and hot paths:\n- Add StorageWriteDebouncer with 100ms write coalescing, replacing\n  per-call tokio::spawn disk writes with batched single-writes\n- Strip osascript subprocess from nativeHost:getCursorScreenPoint,\n  returning (0,0) to eliminate ~50ms macOS process spawn per invocation\n- Gate logger info/debug/trace to opt-in vscode-log tag; forward\n  error/warn/critical to dev_log consistently\n- Replace SystemTime-based ID generation with atomic sequence counters\n  in Notification and WindowUI, eliminating syscall overhead\n\nUpdate Tauri ACL manifests with the new tray allow-set-icon-with-as-template\npermission.",
			"SHA": "e2e1d1e1b9088429512644b8901afcf9dd8d2347"
		},
